ew": "Incumbent Democrat Maggie Goodlander faces a rematch against Republican Lily Tang Williams in New Hampshire's 2nd District, which leans Democratic by about two points. Recent polling from UNH and Saint Anselm shows Goodlander ahead by 15 to 21 points among likely voters, consistent with her 2024 victory over Williams. Expert raters uniformly place the race at Likely D or better, and prediction markets price her chances near 95 percent.\n\nGoodlander has also built a substantial financial advantage, raising over $4 million and holding $2.7 million on hand compared with roughly $1.2 million raised for Williams, who has drawn little outside support. Endorsements such as the Professional Firefighters of New Hampshire add to her position. The race remains Safe Democratic, with the main question being the size of the margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9818, "margin": 13.85}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9772, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.978, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9795, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9872, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9903, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9731, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 15.0}]}